# Store and check out every file byte-for-byte, with no line-ending
# translation.  This matters here for three reasons:
#
#   * the regression suite compares generated SMF against recorded SHA-256
#     hashes, so the sample/*.mml inputs must not change between checkouts;
#   * doc/ and sample/*.txt are legacy Japanese text (Shift-JIS) and
#     sample/*.mml are EUC-JP -- leave the distributed bytes alone;
#   * test/run-baseline.sh and src/makefile must keep LF endings to work
#     under POSIX shells and make, including from WSL on a Windows checkout.
#
# Without this, a checkout with core.autocrlf=true would rewrite all of the
# above to CRLF.
* -text

# Explicitly binary, so Git never tries to diff or merge them as text.
*.mid binary
